{"schema":1,"kind":"decision","id":"01KXPH5EP8XFMVFNDBK4H5D6A7","title":"Add a versioned signed ledger checkpoint","decision":"Keep legacy tip attestations readable and add SignedCheckpoint v2 as a parallel contract with fixed binary signing bytes, a genesis-derived ledger identity, signed tree size/root/tip/timestamp, and an operator-held threshold policy.","alternatives":[{"option":"Mutate LedgerAttestation v1 in place","why_rejected":"would break existing receipt bytes and blur compatibility"},{"option":"Sign generic JSON","why_rejected":"field ordering and serializer behavior are not a stable cryptographic contract"},{"option":"Persist a random store UUID","why_rejected":"would make backup and restore identity depend on mutable side metadata instead of the authoritative ledger"}],"scope":["crates/nahuali-core/src/checkpoint.rs","crates/nahuali-cli/src/commands/checkpoint.rs","crates/nahuali-cli/src/cli.rs"],"commits":["97b6bd0a04b23fb77210190dba802e7b4082007c"],"author":"codex","confidence":"medium","tags":[],"ts":1784241371848}

{"schema":1,"kind":"decision","id":"01KXPJ564VB5ZYSABMV0R65GKR","title":"Add compact Merkle consistency proofs without changing v1 roots","decision":"Keep nahuali-merkle-v1 leaf and node hashing byte-for-byte unchanged, and add an RFC-9162-shaped consistency proof over that existing tree so verifiers can prove append-only growth from two roots and sizes without the ledger.","alternatives":[{"option":"Replace the historical tree with RFC 9162 hashing","why_rejected":"rejected because every existing Merkle root and receipt would change"},{"option":"Keep only full-prefix replay","why_rejected":"rejected because remote witnesses and offline receipts would still need the complete ledger"}],"scope":["crates/nahuali-core/src/merkle.rs","crates/nahuali-core/src/lib.rs"],"commits":["97b6bd0a04b23fb77210190dba802e7b4082007c"],"author":"codex","confidence":"medium","tags":[],"ts":1784242411675}
